---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout
  title="Hydrogen Embrittlement in Aerospace Engine Valves — Alejandro Riaño-Molina"
  description="Phase Field Damage Model (PFDM) combined with HEDE and HELP mechanisms to analyze hydrogen-induced failure in aerospace structural components."
  lang="en"
>
  <nav id="navbar">
    <a href="/" class="nav-logo">ARM<span>.</span></a>
    <ul class="nav-links">
      <li><a href="/#projects">Projects</a></li>
      <li><a href="/#contact">Contact</a></li>
      <li><a href="/es/projects/hydrogen-embrittlement" class="lang-toggle"><span class="current">EN</span> / ES</a></li>
    </ul>
  </nav>

  <main class="project-page">
    <a href="/#projects" class="project-back"><span>←</span><span>Back to projects</span></a>

    <div class="section-tag">Project 01 · 2023–2024</div>
    <h1>Hydrogen Embrittlement in Aerospace Engine Valves</h1>
    <p class="hero-sub" style="opacity:1; animation:none; max-width:720px; margin-top:1rem;">
      A phase field framework for predicting hydrogen-induced failure in structural components of liquid-propellant rocket engines.
    </p>

    <div class="project-meta">
      <div class="project-meta-item"><span class="label">Institution</span><span class="value">UNAL · GIDA Group</span></div>
      <div class="project-meta-item"><span class="label">Role</span><span class="value">Aerospace Research Assistant</span></div>
      <div class="project-meta-item"><span class="label">Tools</span><span class="value">MOOSE · C++ · ParaView</span></div>
      <div class="project-meta-item"><span class="label">Output</span><span class="value">IAC 2024 · CEC 2023</span></div>
    </div>

    <!--
      MAIN IMAGE / VIDEO:
      Place a hero image at /public/images/projects/hydrogen-hero.jpg
      (1600×900 recommended — ParaView render of crack propagation, mesh,
      or phase field damage variable d ∈ [0,1] across the geometry).
      Or use a short looping video at /public/videos/hydrogen-loop.mp4.
    -->
    <div class="project-hero-media placeholder" data-label="Place a ParaView render of the phase field damage variable here · /images/projects/hydrogen-hero.jpg">
      <img src="/images/projects/hydrogen-hero.jpg" alt="Phase field damage simulation" onerror="this.style.display='none'" />
    </div>

    <div class="project-section">
      <h3>Context</h3>
      <p>
        Hydrogen embrittlement (HE) is a long-standing failure mode in metallic components exposed to gaseous or
        dissolved hydrogen — particularly relevant in liquid-propellant rocket engines, where valves and turbopumps
        operate under high pressure and cryogenic conditions. Predicting HE-driven crack initiation and propagation
        is still a hard problem because it couples diffusion, stress fields, and microstructural damage mechanisms.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="project-section">
      <h3>Approach</h3>
      <p>
        I implemented a coupled <strong>phase field damage model (PFDM)</strong> incorporating two of the dominant
        embrittlement mechanisms reported in the literature:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>HEDE</strong> (Hydrogen-Enhanced Decohesion) — local reduction of cohesive strength.</li>
        <li><strong>HELP</strong> (Hydrogen-Enhanced Localized Plasticity) — shielding of dislocations, promoting localized softening.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        The implementation was built on the <strong>MOOSE Framework</strong> (C++), solving the coupled
        displacement / damage / hydrogen-concentration system with finite elements.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="project-gallery">
      <div class="project-hero-media placeholder" data-label="/images/projects/hydrogen-mesh.jpg · FE mesh">
        <img src="/images/projects/hydrogen-mesh.jpg" alt="Finite element mesh" onerror="this.style.display='none'" />
      </div>
      <div class="project-hero-media placeholder" data-label="/images/projects/hydrogen-result.jpg · Damage field">
        <img src="/images/projects/hydrogen-result.jpg" alt="Damage field result" onerror="this.style.display='none'" />
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="project-section">
      <h3>Outcome</h3>
      <p>
        The framework reproduced the qualitative crack-path behavior reported in experimental studies on
        hydrogen-charged steels, and was the basis for two conference contributions (IAC Milan 2024, CEC 2023)
        and my undergraduate thesis at Universidad Nacional de Colombia.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="project-section">
      <h3>What I'd improve</h3>
      <p>
        The current model assumes isotropic hydrogen diffusion and a single damage variable. A natural next step
        would be to incorporate trap-controlled diffusion and a microstructure-informed phase field, and to validate
        against in-situ hydrogen-charging experiments with full-field DIC.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="project-next">
      <a href="/#projects">← All projects</a>
      <a href="/projects/energetic-materials">Next: Energetic Materials →</a>
    </div>
  </main>

  <footer>
    <span class="footer-text">Alejandro Riaño-Molina <span>·</span> Ann Arbor, MI</span>
    <span class="footer-text">Built with Astro <span>·</span> Hosted on GitHub Pages</span>
  </footer>

  <script is:inline>
    const navbar = document.getElementById('navbar');
    window.addEventListener('scroll', () => {
      navbar.classList.toggle('scrolled', window.scrollY > 40);
    });
  </script>
</Layout>
